{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PREMISE RE-VERIFIED against run 31535962079 raw log — the 'benign noise' reading is REFUTED. 'command cancelled' is not noise: it is a silently miscounted FAILURE.\n\nDECISIVE EVIDENCE (run 31535962079):\n  - occurrences of 'ACLI stderr: X Error: command cancelled' = 15\n  - sum of every links_applied= across the whole pass          = 15\n  - occurrences of 'update_one: ... failed'                    = 0\n\nThe correspondence is exact and per-ticket, not just in aggregate:\n  2 cancellations -> REB-1305 links_applied=2; 1 -> REB-1308 links_applied=1;\n  2 -> REB-1398 links_applied=2; 2 -> REB-1442 links_applied=2; 1 -> REB-1538/1656/1666\n  links_applied=1; 2 -> REB-1694 links_applied=2; 1 -> REB-184/2114/2321 links_applied=1.\nEvery ticket with zero cancellations reports links_applied=0.\n\nMECHANISM (dispatch_one.py:778-789, _update_one_dispatch_links):\n\n    try:\n        _call_with_retry(client.delete_issue_link, link_id)\n        _links_applied += 1\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError:\n        # ...treated as idempotent 404/409...\n        _links_applied += 1\n\nThat arm has NO print, which is exactly why zero 'update_one: ... failed' lines appear: the\ngeneric except-Exception arms never fire. The only trace a cancelled delete leaves is\n_run_acli's retry-exhausted 'ACLI stderr:' print (acli_subprocess.py:449-451). The arm then\ncounts the failure as an applied link.\n\nSo links_applied=N in these runs is entirely FABRICATED FROM FAILURES. Zero links were\nactually removed in that pass, and batch_outcome reported error=None with a nonzero\nlinks_applied for every one. This is the bug 44de silent-divergence class, and it is why\nREBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP cannot catch it: the canary tests computed>0 and applied==0,\nand this arm inflates applied to equal computed.\n\nIt is correctly NON-TERMINATING (stinkpot is right that it killed zero runs; those 6 died\nlater in git delivery). But the code comment justifying the arm — 'self-healing, the differ\nrecomputes the REMOVE from managed_refs next pass' — does not hold here: the cause is\nDETERMINISTIC (EOF on stdin at a confirmation prompt, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL), so every\nfuture pass cancels identically. The links are never removed and every pass reports success.\nThat is permanent silent divergence, not transient noise.\n\nROOT CAUSE now has same-repo prior art (surfaced by the plan reviewer, verified): acli.py:714-724\nalready passes --yes to 'workitem delete' because 'without it, acli jira workitem delete waits\non stdin for confirmation and exits non-zero in non-TTY contexts (bug 3256-f960-4ae6-4943,\nsurfaced by the live cfd6 capability probe)'. That is the IDENTICAL failure mode. 'link create'\nand 'link delete' pass neither --json nor --yes. The ticket's original caution conflated --yes\nwith --json: story 25ae proved --json is rejected on those subcommands; it says nothing about\n--yes, which is proven-accepted on a sibling subcommand.\n\nVERDICT: not_a_bug is wrong; pure log-labelling is insufficient (labelling a fabricated\nsuccess as 'benign' would harden the lie). Awaiting coordinator direction on scope."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786525744711036001,"uuid":"971181be-2604-4dee-aa5e-4a9268b81cb1"}